From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] soc: samsung: program the Exynos5433 G3D body bias with
 pd_g3d

The PMU register BB_CON4 (PMU + 0x0790) sets the adaptive body bias of
the G3D (Mali) block.  Mainline never writes it: on the SM-T715 it keeps
the bootloader's 0x8000008d, the reverse bias the stock kernel applies
only while the GPU idles, so the GPU has been running with less timing
margin than under stock.  Stock runs it at 0x80000088 (level 8,
ABB_X100, no bias).

New built-in driver exynos5433-g3d-abb: a node under the PMU, inside
pd_g3d, adds a genpd power notifier to the domain and writes, through
the PMU syscon regmap,

  GENPD_NOTIFY_PRE_ON  the "on" level, before the PMU powers the block
                       up and before any device of the domain resumes
                       (panfrost's runtime resume, the CMU restore);
  GENPD_NOTIFY_OFF     the "off" level, once the block is gated.

So the GPU is never powered with the idle value, and the register holds
stock's idle value whenever the domain is off, as under stock: the Mali
platform code writes the running level before pm_runtime_resume() and
G3D_RBB_VALUE before the runtime suspend (gpu_notifier.c:180-182,
204-206, gpu_exynos5433.c:41,635-668 of kernel_universal5433).  A failed
power-on is followed by OFF (off level back), a failed power-off by ON
(on level still there).  At probe the domain is on (platform bus attach)
and held by the device's disabled runtime PM; the driver writes the on
level, then enables runtime PM in the suspended state, so the node never
holds the domain.

Encoding: (1 << 31) | (1 << 7) | level, 0 for ABB_BYPASS (cal_set_abb(),
asv-exynos5433_cal.c:484-495).  The levels are board properties because
the on level depends on the ASV table: this chip (table version 8, G3D
group 1, stock boot logs) uses abb_table_g3d_v3, 8 at every level
(asv-exynos5433.h:344-355); the off level is G3D_RBB_VALUE 0x8d = 13.
Observable in dmesg (probe line, rate-limited line per transition) and
in /sys/kernel/debug/exynos5433-g3d-abb (register, levels, counts).

The board keeps its 420 MHz GPU cap until a device test has checked the
bias and the faster levels; its comment is updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts     |  35 +++
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig         |  18 ++
 drivers/soc/samsung/Kconfig                   |  14 +
 drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile                  |   2 +
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c      | 239 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 308 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
index eb920a9fd..0ad80dbfb 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
@@ -874,6 +874,41 @@ &framebuffer {
  * "Mali-T760 MC6 (Panfrost)" GLES 3.1 renderer in phoc, no GPU faults.
  */
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi"
+/*
+ * G3D adaptive body bias (docs/GPU.md section 10.12).  The PMU register
+ * BB_CON4 (PMU + 0x0790) biases the GPU block; mainline left the
+ * bootloader's 0x8000008d there, the reverse bias stock applies only
+ * while the GPU idles.  drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c writes
+ * the "on" level before pd_g3d powers on and the "off" level once it is
+ * off, as stock does around the GPU's power-up and idle
+ * (kernel_universal5433 drivers/gpu/arm/t7xx/r22p0/platform/exynos/
+ * gpu_notifier.c:180-182,204-206; gpu_exynos5433.c:635-668).  Register
+ * value: (1 << 31) | (1 << 7) | level (cal_set_abb(),
+ * arch/arm/mach-exynos/asv-exynos5433_cal.c:484-495).
+ *
+ * on: 8 = ABB_X100 (mach/asv-exynos5_cal.h:108), 0x80000088.  This chip
+ *   has ASV table version 8 and G3D group 1 (stock boot logs: "ASV Table
+ *   Ver : 8", "[G3D] DEVFREQ: ...Khz, ABB 8" at all eight levels), so
+ *   stock takes abb_table_g3d_v3 (asv-exynos5433_cal.c:443-449), which is
+ *   8 at every frequency and group (mach/asv-exynos5433.h:344-355).  Table
+ *   versions 0-4 would give ABB_BYPASS (255) instead.  The table path is
+ *   the one in use: the same logs show ABB 255 and 8 at different ARM
+ *   levels, which fused ABB (one 4-bit value per rail,
+ *   asv-exynos5433_cal.c:456-471) cannot give.
+ * off: 13 = ABB_X125 (mach/asv-exynos5_cal.h:113), 0x8000008d: stock's
+ *   G3D_RBB_VALUE 0x8d (gpu_exynos5433.c:41), masked to 5 bits.
+ *
+ * The node sits in pd_g3d only for the notifier: it has runtime PM
+ * enabled and stays suspended, so it never holds the domain on.
+ */
+&pmu_system_controller {
+	gpu-abb {
+		compatible = "samsung,exynos5433-g3d-abb";
+		power-domains = <&pd_g3d>;
+		samsung,abb-on-level = <8>;
+		samsung,abb-off-level = <13>;
+	};
+};
 
 /* ==================================================================== */
 /* 13. Bluetooth (BCM4358 on UART3, hci_bcm)                            */
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index 15155793a..f1a5783d4 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -183,6 +183,24 @@ CONFIG_RMI4_F12=y
 # RECOVERY again).  Loaded by hand / by the initramfs after the guard.
 CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST=m
 
+# GPU frequency scaling: panfrost devfreq over the board's OPP table, on
+# the G3D bus clock (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi, 100 to 400 MHz).
+# PM_DEVFREQ is also selected by panfrost and selects PM_OPP.  panfrost's
+# governor built in, so devfreq_add_device() needs no request_module() at
+# panfrost load (drivers/devfreq/devfreq.c); the devfreq cooling device,
+# without which the GPU cooling-map never binds
+# (include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h stub).
+CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ=y
+CONFIG_DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND=y
+CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y
+
+# G3D adaptive body bias (docs/GPU.md section 10.12): stock's no-bias
+# level in PMU BB_CON4 whenever pd_g3d is on, its idle reverse bias while
+# it is off (board node &pmu_system_controller/gpu-abb).  Built in, so it
+# is bound before the panfrost module powers the GPU up; its probe only
+# touches an always-on PMU register.
+CONFIG_EXYNOS5433_G3D_ABB=y
+
 # Requested by the Omarchy (Hyprland) track, built in because the rootfs
 # ships no modules.  Firewall for ufw / iptables-nft (omarchy-mobile's
 # kernel fragment):
diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/samsung/Kconfig
index 26d05f1b7..1b2b45a20 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/Kconfig
@@ -72,6 +72,20 @@ config SAMSUNG_PM_CHECK_CHUNKSIZE
 	  the CRC data block will take more memory, but will identify any
 	  faults with better precision.
 
+config EXYNOS5433_G3D_ABB
+	bool "Exynos5433 G3D adaptive body bias"
+	depends on ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS && OF
+	select MFD_SYSCON
+	help
+	  Program the body bias of the Exynos5433 GPU block (PMU register
+	  BB_CON4) from the G3D power domain: a "samsung,exynos5433-g3d-abb"
+	  node under the PMU gives one level for while the domain is on and
+	  one for while it is off.  Mainline otherwise leaves the
+	  bootloader's value, which on the Samsung SM-T715 is the reverse
+	  bias the stock kernel uses only for an idle GPU.  Built in, so that
+	  it is bound before the GPU driver powers the domain up.
+
 config EXYNOS_REGULATOR_COUPLER
 	bool "Exynos SoC Regulator Coupler" if COMPILE_TEST
 	depends on ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST
diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile b/drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile
index 3d4934da6..768587480 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_EXYNOS_PMU_ARM_DRIVERS)	+= exynos3250-pmu.o exynos4-pmu.o \
 					exynos5250-pmu.o exynos5420-pmu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_EXYNOS_REGULATOR_COUPLER) += exynos-regulator-coupler.o
 
+obj-$(CONFIG_EXYNOS5433_G3D_ABB)	+= exynos5433-g3d-abb.o
+
 obj-$(CONFIG_SAMSUNG_PM_CHECK)	+= s3c-pm-check.o
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_SAMSUNG_SEC_LOG_CONSOLE) += sec-log-console.o
diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b92010bc0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos5433-g3d-abb.c
@@ -0,0 +1,239 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Exynos5433 G3D adaptive body bias (ABB), switched with the G3D power
+ * domain.
+ *
+ * The PMU register BB_CON4 (PMU + 0x0790) sets the body bias of the G3D
+ * (Mali GPU) block.  Mainline never programs it, so the GPU runs with
+ * whatever the bootloader left there; on the SM-T715 that is 0x8000008d,
+ * the reverse body bias the stock kernel applies only while the GPU idles.
+ * Stock runs the GPU at 0x80000088 (level 8, no bias).
+ *
+ * This driver binds to a node that sits in pd_g3d and adds a genpd power
+ * notifier to it: the "on" level is written before the domain powers on
+ * (GENPD_NOTIFY_PRE_ON) and the "off" level after it has powered off
+ * (GENPD_NOTIFY_OFF).  The GPU block is therefore never powered with the
+ * "off" level, and the register holds the stock idle value whenever the
+ * domain is off.  The levels come from the device tree, because the "on"
+ * level depends on the chip's ASV table version.
+ *
+ * Stock references (Samsung kernel for the SM-T715, kernel_universal5433):
+ *
+ *  - register: abb_base_arr[SYSC_DVFS_G3D] = CHIPID_ABBG_BASE + 0x0790
+ *    (arch/arm/mach-exynos/asv-exynos5433_cal.c:26), CHIPID_ABBG_BASE =
+ *    S5P_VA_CHIPID5 (mach/asv-exynos5_cal.h:42), mapped from
+ *    EXYNOS_PA_CHIPID5 0x105C0000 (mach/map.h:79, mach-exynos/common.c:885-889),
+ *    which is the PMU (EXYNOS5430_PA_PMU, mach/map.h:87); the PMU header
+ *    names it EXYNOS5433_BB_CON4 (mach/regs-pmu-exynos5433.h:46).
+ *  - encoding: cal_set_abb() writes 0 for ABB_BYPASS, otherwise
+ *    (1 << 31) | (1 << 7) | (level & 0x1f) (asv-exynos5433_cal.c:484-495);
+ *    BIT(31) | BIT(7) is EXYNOS_ABB_INIT (mach/regs-pmu.h:104).  Levels:
+ *    ABB_X060 = 0 ... ABB_X100 = 8 ... ABB_X125 = 13 ... ABB_X160 = 20,
+ *    ABB_BYPASS = 255 (mach/asv-exynos5_cal.h:100-121).
+ *  - when: the Mali platform code writes the level of the current DVFS step
+ *    (gpu_dvfs_get_cur_asv_abb()) when the GPU leaves DVS, before
+ *    pm_runtime_resume() powers it up (drivers/gpu/arm/t7xx/r22p0/platform/
+ *    exynos/gpu_notifier.c:180-182, gpu_exynos5433.c:658-668), and
+ *    G3D_RBB_VALUE 0x8d (level 13) when it enters DVS on idle, before the
+ *    runtime suspend that powers it down (gpu_notifier.c:204-206,219-221,
+ *    gpu_exynos5433.c:41,635-652).  Both are skipped on chips with fused
+ *    ABB (cal_get_fs_abb(), asv-exynos5433_cal.c:110-115).
+ */
+
+#include <linux/bits.h>
+#include <linux/debugfs.h>
+#include <linux/device.h>
+#include <linux/err.h>
+#include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
+#include <linux/mod_devicetable.h>
+#include <linux/notifier.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_domain.h>
+#include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
+#include <linux/regmap.h>
+#include <linux/seq_file.h>
+
+#define EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4	0x0790
+
+#define ABB_ENABLE		(BIT(31) | BIT(7))
+#define ABB_LEVEL_MASK		GENMASK(4, 0)
+#define ABB_LEVEL_MAX		20	/* ABB_X160 */
+#define ABB_LEVEL_BYPASS	255	/* ABB_BYPASS: register 0 */
+
+struct g3d_abb {
+	struct device *dev;
+	struct regmap *pmu;
+	struct notifier_block nb;
+	u32 on_val;
+	u32 off_val;
+	unsigned int on_count;
+	unsigned int off_count;
+};
+
+static int g3d_abb_set(struct g3d_abb *abb, u32 val, const char *why)
+{
+	u32 old = 0;
+	int ret;
+
+	regmap_read(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, &old);
+	ret = regmap_write(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, val);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(abb->dev, "%s: cannot write BB_CON4: %d\n", why, ret);
+	else
+		dev_info_ratelimited(abb->dev, "%s: BB_CON4 0x%08x -> 0x%08x\n",
+				     why, old, val);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Called by genpd with the domain lock held (drivers/pmdomain/core.c,
+ * _genpd_power_on() and _genpd_power_off()).  PRE_ON comes before the PMU
+ * powers the block on, and before any device of the domain is resumed
+ * (genpd_runtime_resume() powers the domain on before the driver's
+ * callback), so the GPU never runs with the "off" level.  A failed power-on
+ * is followed by OFF, which puts the "off" level back.  A failed power-off
+ * is followed by ON, with the "on" level still in place.
+ */
+static int g3d_abb_notify(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long action,
+			  void *data)
+{
+	struct g3d_abb *abb = container_of(nb, struct g3d_abb, nb);
+
+	switch (action) {
+	case GENPD_NOTIFY_PRE_ON:
+		abb->on_count++;
+		return notifier_from_errno(g3d_abb_set(abb, abb->on_val,
+						       "pd_g3d power-on"));
+	case GENPD_NOTIFY_OFF:
+		abb->off_count++;
+		g3d_abb_set(abb, abb->off_val, "pd_g3d power-off");
+		return NOTIFY_OK;
+	default:
+		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+	}
+}
+
+static int g3d_abb_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
+{
+	struct g3d_abb *abb = s->private;
+	u32 val;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, &val);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	seq_printf(s, "bb_con4: 0x%08x\n", val);
+	seq_printf(s, "on: 0x%08x\n", abb->on_val);
+	seq_printf(s, "off: 0x%08x\n", abb->off_val);
+	seq_printf(s, "power_on_count: %u\n", abb->on_count);
+	seq_printf(s, "power_off_count: %u\n", abb->off_count);
+	return 0;
+}
+DEFINE_SHOW_ATTRIBUTE(g3d_abb);
+
+static int g3d_abb_read_level(struct device *dev, const char *prop, u32 *val)
+{
+	u32 level;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = device_property_read_u32(dev, prop, &level);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "missing %s\n", prop);
+
+	if (level == ABB_LEVEL_BYPASS) {
+		*val = 0;
+		return 0;
+	}
+	if (level > ABB_LEVEL_MAX)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "%s: level %u out of range\n",
+				     prop, level);
+
+	*val = ABB_ENABLE | (level & ABB_LEVEL_MASK);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Built in and never unbound (suppress_bind_attrs): the notifier and the
+ * debugfs file stay for the kernel's lifetime, so nothing is undone on
+ * remove.  The notifier is not device-managed: on a probe failure the
+ * platform bus detaches the domain before devres runs, and the notifier
+ * could no longer be found to unregister it.
+ */
+static int g3d_abb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct g3d_abb *abb;
+	u32 old = 0;
+	int ret;
+
+	abb = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*abb), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!abb)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	abb->dev = dev;
+
+	/* The node is a child of the PMU system controller. */
+	if (!dev->parent || !dev->parent->of_node)
+		return -ENODEV;
+	abb->pmu = syscon_node_to_regmap(dev->parent->of_node);
+	if (IS_ERR(abb->pmu))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(abb->pmu), "no PMU regmap\n");
+
+	ret = g3d_abb_read_level(dev, "samsung,abb-on-level", &abb->on_val);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = g3d_abb_read_level(dev, "samsung,abb-off-level", &abb->off_val);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The platform bus has attached this device to pd_g3d and powered the
+	 * domain on (drivers/base/platform.c, dev_pm_domain_attach()).  Runtime
+	 * PM is still disabled, which genpd counts as an active device
+	 * (genpd_power_off(), pm_runtime_suspended()), so the domain stays on
+	 * until runtime PM is enabled below: the notifier and the "on" level
+	 * are in place before it can toggle.
+	 */
+	abb->nb.notifier_call = g3d_abb_notify;
+	ret = dev_pm_genpd_add_notifier(dev, &abb->nb);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "cannot add a pd_g3d notifier\n");
+
+	regmap_read(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, &old);
+	ret = regmap_write(abb->pmu, EXYNOS5433_PMU_BB_CON4, abb->on_val);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_pm_genpd_remove_notifier(dev);
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "cannot write BB_CON4\n");
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Runtime PM enabled in its initial suspended state: this device no
+	 * longer holds the domain, and genpd may power it off once the driver
+	 * core has synced it after probe (genpd_dev_pm_sync()).  The device
+	 * has no runtime PM callbacks and never resumes.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
+
+	debugfs_create_file("exynos5433-g3d-abb", 0444, NULL, abb,
+			    &g3d_abb_fops);
+
+	dev_info(dev, "G3D ABB 0x%08x while pd_g3d is on, 0x%08x while off; BB_CON4 was 0x%08x, now 0x%08x\n",
+		 abb->on_val, abb->off_val, old, abb->on_val);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct of_device_id g3d_abb_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "samsung,exynos5433-g3d-abb" },
+	{ }
+};
+
+static struct platform_driver g3d_abb_driver = {
+	.probe = g3d_abb_probe,
+	.driver = {
+		.name = "exynos5433-g3d-abb",
+		.of_match_table = g3d_abb_of_match,
+		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
+	},
+};
+builtin_platform_driver(g3d_abb_driver);
-- 
